---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { SITE, withBase } from "../lib/site";

const effectiveDate = "September 2, 2026";
const sections = [
  ["overview", "Overview"],
  ["information", "Information we process"],
  ["services", "Third-party services"],
  ["advertising", "Advertising"],
  ["retention", "Retention and choices"],
  ["rights", "Your privacy rights"],
  ["children", "Children"],
  ["security", "Security and transfers"],
  ["changes", "Changes and contact"],
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How NutCracker Tools handles app settings, Firebase analytics and diagnostics, advertising, notifications, and website data."
  page="privacy"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero__inner shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</span>
      <h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1>
      <p>This policy explains the limited information handled by NutCracker Tools, its service providers, and this website.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__meta">
        <span class="chip chip--warm">Effective · {effectiveDate}</span>
        <span class="chip">Android · {SITE.packageName}</span>
        <span class="chip chip--teal">No app account required</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section section--flush-top">
    <div class="legal-layout shell">
      <nav class="legal-nav aside-card" aria-label="Privacy policy contents">
        <strong>On this page</strong>
        <ul>{sections.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}</ul>
      </nav>

      <article class="legal-content">
        <div class="legal-intro">
          <p><strong>Summary:</strong> NutCracker Tools has no user-account system. Basic settings and recent activity are kept on your device. Connected features use Google Firebase, and the app may show Google Mobile Ads after the applicable consent process. This website does not use analytics or advertising trackers.</p>
        </div>

        <section class="legal-section" id="overview">
          <h2>1. Overview and scope</h2>
          <p>{SITE.operator} (“we,” “us,” or “our”) provides NutCracker Tools, Android package <strong>{SITE.packageName}</strong>, and this companion website. This policy explains what information is processed, why it is processed, and the choices available to you.</p>
          <p>The app does not create user profiles or ask for your name, email address, precise location, contacts, photos, financial information, or biometric information.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="information">
          <h2>2. Information we process</h2>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="legal-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>App settings and activity</td><td>Preferences, saved items, and recent activity</td><td>Provide app features and remember your choices</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Analytics and diagnostics</td><td>Feature usage, app version, installation identifiers, crash details, and performance information</td><td>Improve reliability and understand general usage</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Advertising</td><td>Consent choices, ad interactions, and advertising signals where allowed</td><td>Deliver, measure, and protect ads</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Optional notifications</td><td>Firebase installation and registration identifiers after opt-in</td><td>Send announcements and important notices</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Website data</td><td>Theme preferences and standard hosting request information</td><td>Operate and secure this website</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>Our custom analytics events are designed not to include free-form content, credentials, or authentication tokens. Firebase may process standard app, device, network, and installation information under Google’s documentation and settings.</p>
          <p>This website does not use website analytics, ad pixels, account cookies, or a form backend. GitHub Pages may process standard request information for hosting, security, and abuse prevention. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="services">
          <h2>3. Third-party services</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Google Firebase:</strong> Analytics, Crashlytics, Performance Monitoring, Remote Config, Firebase Installations, and optional Cloud Messaging.</li>
            <li><strong>Google advertising services:</strong> AdMob/Google Mobile Ads, User Messaging Platform, and related advertising partners.</li>
            <li><strong>Connected services:</strong> External APIs and content-delivery providers used by connected app features.</li>
            <li><strong>Website hosting:</strong> GitHub Pages.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These providers may receive the information needed to provide their services, along with standard technical details such as IP address, device or browser type, language, and timestamps. Their own privacy policies also apply.</p>
          <p>Learn more from <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Firebase Privacy and Security</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="advertising">
          <h2>4. Advertising and consent</h2>
          <p>NutCracker Tools may show banner, interstitial, and app-open ads. The app uses Google’s User Messaging Platform to request consent where required before Google Mobile Ads begins requesting ads.</p>
          <p>Depending on your location and choices, ads may be personalized, non-personalized, limited, or used only for technical delivery. Where available, you can review your ad-privacy choices from the app’s Settings. See Google’s <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy">AdMob privacy guidance</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="retention">
          <h2>5. Retention and choices</h2>
          <p>App settings and recent activity remain on your device until you change them, clear the app’s data, or uninstall the app. Website preferences remain in your browser until you clear this site’s data.</p>
          <p>Google and GitHub apply their own retention periods to information they process. You can change notification and available ad-privacy choices in the app, use Google’s privacy controls, and clear app or website data through your device or browser settings.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="rights">
          <h2>6. Your privacy rights</h2>
          <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request a copy, correction, deletion, restriction, objection, portability, or information about certain processing, and to withdraw consent where processing relies on consent.</p>
          <p>To make a privacy request, start through our <a href={withBase("support/")}>Support page</a>. Do not post personal information, device identifiers, or credentials in the public issue tracker.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="children">
          <h2>7. Children’s privacy</h2>
          <p>NutCracker Tools is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly seek personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us through the Support page.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="security">
          <h2>8. Security and international processing</h2>
          <p>We use reasonable platform and service-provider safeguards, but no method of processing or transmission is completely secure.</p>
          <p>Google, GitHub, and other connected service providers may process information in countries other than your own, subject to their terms, safeguards, and applicable law.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="changes">
          <h2>9. Changes and contact</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy when the app, website, service providers, legal requirements, or privacy controls change. We will revise the effective date when we do.</p>
          <p>Questions can be started through the <a href={withBase("support/")}>NutCracker Tools Support page</a> or the <a href={SITE.issues}>project issue tracker</a>. Do not place sensitive information in a public issue.</p>
          <p><strong>Operator:</strong> {SITE.operator}<br /><strong>Product:</strong> {SITE.name}<br /><strong>Android package:</strong> {SITE.packageName}<br /><strong>Effective date:</strong> {effectiveDate}</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
